{"_id":"6a2fec612204ffbc59e5a1ba","roadmapSlug":"python-data-analysis","nodeId":"Md0yXC3JTH56Wky5jA8Fk","description":"# Comparison\n\nComparison operators evaluate the relationship between two values and return a boolean. They include `==`, `!=`, `<`, `>`, `<=`, and `>=`. They form the building blocks of filtering conditions applied to DataFrames and arrays.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"Python Comparison Operators","url":"https://www.w3schools.com/python/gloss_python_comparison_operators.asp","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeaf4"},{"type":"video","title":"Comparison Operators in Python","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6ZQtBK-dM9c","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeaf5"}],"createdAt":"2026-06-15T12:13:21.181Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-07T12:44:22.099Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e3360acf8c05faf5e1c2a","title":"DataCamp - Data Analyst with Python","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/QY0dY9"},{"_id":"6a5e3365acf8c05faf5e1ded","title":"DataCamp - Python Data Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/k4V24x"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/python-data-analysis/content/Md0yXC3JTH56Wky5jA8Fk.md"}